::JOUR_U05_L03_GP_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.03] Source: Field Photo Accuracy Check. Assignment: Create accurate visual images for a school news brief about the new water bottle refill station outside the gym. Available Images: Image A shows the actual refill station outside the gym with the blue installation sign visible. Image B shows an older hallway water fountain near the cafeteria. Image C is a close-up of a student filling a bottle, but the station label is cropped out. Image D shows the refill station after the caption writer added the location and date. Reporting Notes: The station opened Monday. The facilities manager said it is the first refill station installed near the gym. The student government sponsor said the project was funded by a campus wellness grant. Accuracy Requirement: The final visual must show the correct station, avoid misleading cropping, and include a caption that identifies what the audience is seeing. Question 1: Which image best supports the refill station report? {
~A. Image B is best because it is an older and familiar water fountain.#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source and identify the visual accuracy, revision, evidence, audience, or publication requirement. Step 2: compare this option with the lesson model. This option is weak because it misleads the audience, ignores source evidence, skips revision, weakens format quality, or does not fit the publication purpose.
~B. Image C is best because cropped images are always more professional.#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source and identify the visual accuracy, revision, evidence, audience, or publication requirement. Step 2: compare this option with the lesson model. This option is weak because it misleads the audience, ignores source evidence, skips revision, weakens format quality, or does not fit the publication purpose.
=C. Image D best supports the report because it shows the correct station and includes location and date context.#Correct. Step 1: identify the production or publication skill in the standard. Step 2: connect the answer to the embedded journalism scenario. This answer works because it protects accuracy, uses evidence, improves clarity, follows format expectations, or supports the intended audience.
~D. Image A should be rejected because installation signs are never useful.#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source and identify the visual accuracy, revision, evidence, audience, or publication requirement. Step 2: compare this option with the lesson model. This option is weak because it misleads the audience, ignores source evidence, skips revision, weakens format quality, or does not fit the publication purpose.
}
